course: dictionary
lesson: 11387
title: Abundant: more than enough
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Abundant means there is a lot of something, more than enough. «The orchard had an abundant crop of apples this year.» The baskets were full and nobody had to go without, so abundant means plentiful.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The rainforest gets abundant rain, so the plants stay green all year.» If you swap in plenty or lots and the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is probably right.
explain: Abundant can also mean rich in something, and it is often followed by in. «The river is abundant in trout.» The trout are the thing there is plenty of.
fact: Abundant is an adjective. Its other forms are more abundant and most abundant.
fact: «Abundant» means existing in large amounts, more than enough.
fact: «Abundant in» means rich in something, as in «abundant in fish».
fact: In science, oxygen is the most abundant element in Earth's crust.
fact: In maths, an abundant number has divisors (not counting itself) that add up to more than the number: 12 is abundant because 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + 6 = 16.
exercise: «The farm had an abundant supply of fresh water.» What does abundant mean? | *More than enough | Very small | Dirty | Hard to find
exercise: «The lake is abundant in trout.» What does abundant in mean here? | Has no trout at all | Has trout that are very small | Is too cold for trout | *Has plenty of trout
exercise: Why is 12 an abundant number? | It is an even number that is easy to halve | 12 is the biggest number in the times table | It has exactly two divisors | *Its divisors, not counting 12, add up to more than 12
test: A good harvest gave the village abundant food. What does abundant mean? | Poisoned | *Plentiful | Rare | Hungry
test: Which phrase means there is plenty of something? | Barely a whisper | *Abundant supply | Ancient castle | Curt reply
exam: Which number is abundant? | 7 | 8 | 5 | *12
